## Why This Is Asked
A real-time streaming pipeline with backpressure and external dependencies tests more than single endpoints; ensures autoscaling correctness and end-to-end latency budgets.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end latency in streaming pipelines
- Backpressure and circuit breakers
- Workload modeling for bursts vs steady-state
- Autoscaling behavior and metrics
- Bottleneck localization across Kafka, enrichment, external API, DB

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple Kafka load generator (pseudo) using kafkajs
const { Kafka } = require('kafkajs');
const kafka = new Kafka({ clientId: 'load', brokers: ['kafka:9092'] });
const producer = kafka.producer();
async function run(n) {
  await producer.connect();
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    await producer.send({ topic: 'fraud', messages: [{ value: JSON.stringify({ id: i, amount: Math.random() * 1000 }) }] });
  }
  await producer.disconnect();
}
run(1000000).catch(console.error);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify backpressure impact on downstream services?
- How would you adapt the test when external API SLA degrades?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design end-to-end performance tests for latency-sensitive, distributed systems that must handle burst traffic while maintaining strict SLAs.

## Key Concepts

- Tail latency (p99) measurement and SLA verification
- Backpressure implementation and queue depth management
- Autoscaling strategies (HPA/KEDA) and rapid scale-up behavior
- Distributed tracing (OpenTelemetry, Jaeger) for latency breakdown analysis
- Cold-start impact assessment in mixed serverless/Kubernetes environments

## Code Example

```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
import { Rate } from 'k6/metrics';

const errorRate = new Rate('errors');

export const options = {
  stages: [
    { duration: '2m', target: 20000 }, // Baseline
    { duration: '2m', target: 40000 }, // 2x burst
    { duration: '2m', target: 80000 }, // 4x stress test
  ],
  thresholds: {
    http_req_duration: ['p(99)<120'],
    errors: ['rate<0.005'],
  },
};

export default function () {
  const response = http.post('https://api.bidding-engine.com/bid', {
    auctionId: Math.random().toString(36),
    bidAmount: Math.floor(Math.random() * 1000),
    timestamp: Date.now(),
  });

  errorRate.add(!check(response, {
    'status is 200': (r) => r.status === 200,
    'response time < 120ms': (r) => r.timings.duration < 120,
  }));

  sleep(0.01);
}
```

